WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.779 --> 00:00:02.850
- [Narrator] In 2021, the IPO pipeline

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.500
was flowing with record volume.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.600
An IPO, or Initial Public Offering,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.520
is the traditional way
a company goes public

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.334
by listing shares on the stock exchange.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.440
And last year, IPOs raised
more money than ever.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.600
- One of the biggest IPOs since Alibaba-

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.863
- [News Anchor] The biggest IPO of 2021-

00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:19.920
- [Narrator] But by
December, a broad selloff

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.470
in high growth stocks led
to 2/3 of those in the US

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.900
trading below their IPO price.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.533
And now, the IPO pipeline
is seemingly frozen.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.800
- We haven't seen this slow a year

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.553
in terms of money raised,
since at least 2009.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.490
- [Narrator] That's
because sky high inflation,

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.250
rising interest rates, and
Russia's invasion of Ukraine,

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.110
have made the financial markets volatile

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.737
and in turn, made investors
wary of risky assets like IPOs.

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:49.170
- [Corrie] Everything that you could think

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.440
of that would make launching
an IPO unpalatable,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.480
like, it was happening.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.040
- [Narrator] And now analysts are worried

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.660
that if it doesn't turn around soon,

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.183
the IPO freeze could carry
over into the new year.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.870
So far this year,
traditional IPOs have raised

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.940
only around $7 billion.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.310
In a typical year, traditional
IPOs would've raised

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.650
around $38 billion by this time.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.750
And at this time last
year, the number was closer

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.700
to 120 billion.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.760
Several major companies,
including two Fintech giants,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.160
had anticipated going public in 2022

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.200
before the pipeline
froze and their valuation

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.640
shriveled up with it.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.363
- It was supposed to be the
year of the Fintech company.

00:01:26.363 --> 00:01:29.902
There were many in the
pipeline ready to go.

00:01:29.902 --> 00:01:31.986
We have not seen them.

00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:34.990
- Klarna Bank AB was one of
those highly anticipated IPOs,

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.186
but instead of making a splashy debut,

00:01:37.186 --> 00:01:39.750
the Sweden-based company
laid off hundreds of workers

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.670
to cut costs and was
forced to seek funding

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.576
in private markets.

00:01:42.576 --> 00:01:46.860
It's more than $45 billion
valuation dropped by 85%

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.659
down to $6.7 billion.

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:51.152
Klarna declined to
comment on its IPO plans.

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:53.850
Instacart also had to slash its valuation.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.245
In this case, by around
70% to $13 billion.

00:01:57.245 --> 00:01:59.970
However, with its growing
revenue, Instacart was

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.620
among a few companies still hoping

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.830
for some heat and the opportunity
to go public this year.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.260
- There's a renewed focus on,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.930
show that you can become profitable.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.941
If not right now, very soon.

00:02:13.941 --> 00:02:16.200
- [Narrator] But the company
reeled back its ambitions

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.400
in late October.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.190
In a memo to employees, Instacart CEO said

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.870
that tumultuous market conditions

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.650
are making an IPO for the
company highly unlikely in 2022.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.210
But one area that has broken

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.280
through the ice this year is spinoffs.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.960
This is when a larger company separates

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.460
one of its subsidiaries or branches

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.530
into a separate public company.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.870
Intel self-driving car unit Mobileye

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.540
is one of those IPOs
expected to come through.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.696
After purchasing the unit
for around $15 billion,

00:02:42.696 --> 00:02:44.904
Intel was expecting a Mobileye valuation

00:02:44.904 --> 00:02:47.550
near $50 billion last year.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.316
But today, Intel's
expecting a target valuation

00:02:50.316 --> 00:02:51.843
under $20 billion.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.050
Intel CEO has said that listing Mobileye

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.540
would give the self-driving
car unit a higher profile

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.950
and attract more business.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.253
He has also said that Intel
doesn't need the money

00:03:00.253 --> 00:03:02.740
Mobileye's IPO would generate.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.010
But Mobileye wouldn't be the first IPO

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.440
in the auto industry to
go public in this weather.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.240
Porsche launched on the Frankfurt Exchange

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.315
at the end of September.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:12.330
Though it's not a US IPO,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.820
many analysts agreed that
if Porsche's went well,

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.532
it would be a positive
sign for the US IPO market.

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:22.071
- However, Porsche's IPO, I
wouldn't call a raging success.

00:03:22.071 --> 00:03:24.905
Yes, it priced at the
high end of its range,

00:03:24.905 --> 00:03:28.140
but shares didn't do very well,

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.940
didn't have a great pop.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.250
- [Narrator] That pop she's
talking about is how bankers

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.350
evaluate their initial pricing strategy.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.300
They look for a pop to show momentum,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.160
but not too big of one
that would signal money

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.370
was left on the table.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.656
Porsche declined to comment on its IPO.

00:03:41.656 --> 00:03:44.370
- [Corrie] The joke is
how you price an IPO.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.650
It's an art, not a science, as they say.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.170
You wanna see shares go up, maybe not.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.510
You definitely don't wanna
see them double the first day,

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.786
but you wanna see them rise.

00:03:53.786 --> 00:03:56.640
- [Narrator] Now, investors
will look for green shoots,

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.440
signals that the market is warming up.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.907
However, the indicators of today

00:03:59.907 --> 00:04:01.825
may look different than recent years.

00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:05.700
- [Corrie] In 2020, 2021,
you could go to market

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.910
with a dream (laughs) and a vision

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.740
of how you were going to make money,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.290
and how you were going to grow so fast.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:17.550
That isn't gonna cut it in 2022 and 2023,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.620
or at least doesn't look
like it will cut it.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.630
- [Narrator] The electric
vehicle truck company Rivian

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.520
is viewed as one of the last big IPOs

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.840
before the market crashed.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.365
It scored a valuation so high

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:28.329
that meant it was more valuable than Ford.

00:04:28.329 --> 00:04:31.406
- [Corrie] We're starting to
see cracks in the US economy.

00:04:31.406 --> 00:04:33.960
Remember, just a couple
weeks after Rivian,

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.200
that's when the stock market
started really shifting

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.730
and selling down a lot.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.740
- [Narrator] Rivian's stock
price has since come down.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.410
The company was hit with a
lawsuit for allegedly misleading

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.780
investors about electric vehicle prices,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.540
and recently, it recalled
around 13,000 vehicles

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:49.656
for loose fasteners.

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:52.890
Rivian did not respond
to a request for comment.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.750
Historically, IPOs are viewed as one

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.610
of the riskiest asset classes.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.530
Because you're investing
in a brand new company,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.121
few have a history of profits.

00:05:00.121 --> 00:05:02.201
However, a flowing IPO pipeline

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.036
means companies are raising more money,

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.850
which can lead to more hiring,

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.100
investing in tech, and
employees finally getting

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.075
to cash in on their stock options.

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:13.500
So what would it take to
thaw the IPO pipeline?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.245
- [Corrie] Success begets success.

00:05:15.245 --> 00:05:19.500
So you just need to see
a string of IPOs do well

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.010
to encourage more companies
to want to go public.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.030
- [Narrator] But even as some look

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.380
to push the pipeline forward,

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.750
the broader financial
market remains volatile.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.520
IPO bankers and lawyers agree.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.290
They say the first companies to go public

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.780
after the markets calm
down should be profitable,

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.949
fairly large and must own names.

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:38.250
It all comes down to appetite for risk.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.200
When investors are comfortable
stomaching that risk,

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.741
the IPO market is strong

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:44.553
and the economy usually
looks stable, as well.

